3.53],[1759276800,-5.82],[1761955200,-0.58],[1764547200,5.79],[1767225600,3.78],[1769904000,1],[1772323200,0.81],[1775001600,3.65],[1777593600,10.76],[1780272000,10.81],[1782864000,9.77],[1785542400,12.17],[1788220800,11.28]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What does the Energy Requirement data represent?","answer":"Energy requirements data represents the total amount of energy required to support various economic activities within the country, indicating industrial and consumer demand for electricity.^This includes energy consumed by households, industries, transportation, and other sectors."},{"question":"What is the significance of the Energy Requirement data?","answer":"It reflects the overall energy demand, which is closely linked to economic activities across all sectors, including industrial, residential, and transport sectors.^This data helps in assessing the efficiency of energy use and the potential need for energy conservation and management strategies.^This data is vital for understanding the dynamics of energy consumption and for planning future energy infrastructure, ensuring energy security, and making informed decisions about energy mix and investments in renewable sources for sustainable energy development."},{"question":"How to interpret the Energy Requirement data?","answer":"Analyse the trends in energy requirements over time to understand the growth patterns and developmental trajectory of the economy.^Assess the relationship between changes in energy requirements and economic growth indicators such as GDP, industrial production, inflation and services sector growth.^Evaluate how changes in energy requirements affect energy prices and, subsequently, the overall inflation rate, considering the cost of energy as a key input for most economic activities."}],"related":[{"slug":"average-daily-electronic-toll-collection","title":"E-Toll Collections (Daily Avg)"},{"slug":"bank-credit-growth","title":"Bank Credit Growth"},{"slug":"capacity-utilisation","title":